- `<R911-DET>` = Read at origin main f3ab00bd473d053a0f925616aebfe550aca3ba64. The two test files and the helper are byte-identical to main 8a812415, the commit this ticket was written against (git blob ids faa6db5c6064a644b32315da59482136af64ae47, 45a2a8906d08fdc82e72524b0421dc54b2bc6fb2 and 2e0f520841d93335c20d715be82ac2c8b58084b9 at both), so the description's pointers still hold. Instrument: a line census over the three files for setTimeout, setInterval, Date.now, performance.now, hrtime, jest.setTimeout, toBeLessThan, toBeGreaterThan, elapsed, deadline, sleep, names ending in _MS or Ms, a number times 1000, timeout, fake-timer calls and a line ending in a bare number of three or more digits (among others); it matched 17 lines in the missing-mid-swap file, 9 in the concurrent-writers file and 5 in the helper, and the same program over a planted file (a Date.now difference under toBeLessThan, a per-test timeout of 90000 and a setTimeout) matched all three planted lines, so a zero would have been visible. toBeLessThan, toBeGreaterThan, fake timers and a per-test timeout argument occur 0 times in the three files. LEFT, nine: (1) __tests__/rd407-r2-missing-mid-swap.test.js:41, jest.setTimeout(60000), the per-cell limit jest allows; left because it limits a hung cell and asserts nothing about speed, and a 60 second stall fails the whole suite in a way no count can express; per-cell run times were not measured. (2) :44, BUDGET, the product's retry budget (JsonStorage.MISSING_RETRY_BUDGET_MS, or 510 when the product has none); left because it is the figure the cells compare against, not a bound on the test's own clock. (3) :246, :253 and :255, cell M2 (t0, elapsed, elapsed >= BUDGET); left because it is a lower bound: a stalled runner makes elapsed longer, which keeps it true, and it turns red only if the product gives up before its budget, which is the defect the cell guards. (4) __tests__/rd407-concurrent-settings-writers.test.js:68, STORM_DEADLINE_MS = 60000, used at :241 and :242 (wait for both writers to print ready) and :253 and :254 (kill both with SIGKILL when passed), one deadline per storm shared by the wait and the storm; left because it is a long deadline and, if it is reached, the CONTROL cell (:294 to :300, which requires exit code 0, every round and no fatal) turns red naming the exit and signal, so the failure is loud; not measured: how long a storm takes on a hosted runner, since a green cell prints no figure, and what S1 and S2 do after a kill. (5) :69, jest.setTimeout(2 * STORMS * 15000 + 120000) with STORMS 8 at :67, which is 360000; left as (1); recorded, not decided: eight storms at the 60000 deadline would be 480000, more than 360000, so jest's limit is reached first if every storm ran to its deadline. (6) :90 and :242, sleep(20), a 20 millisecond poll cadence; left because it is a cadence, not a bound. (7) :504, FUTURE, now plus 3600 * 1000, used at :525 as a session expiry handed to the product; left because only a stall of an hour would matter and no test clock compares against it. (8) __tests__/helpers/rd407-setting-writer.js:75, setTimeout(tick, 2), a 2 millisecond poll for the go file; left as a cadence. (9) the same helper at :83 and :97, started = Date.now() and ms: Date.now() - started, reported in the writer's result and never asserted (the field ms occurs 0 times in the concurrent-writers test file); left. CANDIDATE FOR A COUNT, tenth, not done here: __tests__/rd407-r2-missing-mid-swap.test.js:45, PAST_BUDGET_MS = BUDGET + 400, with missingName at :128, the clock check at :138 (Date.now() minus startedAt greater than forMs) and its start at :139, used at :245 (M2), :319 (R1) and :344 (R3), each of which expects the store to read as unreadable after the window. The window ends by the wall clock, so a stall of more than about 400 milliseconds inside the product's retry loop can end the injected miss before the product spends its budget, the read then succeeds and the cell turns red; this is an inference from the source, not a measurement, as the ticket says. The helper already has a counted mode, observations, which cell R2 uses at :330, but how many observations the retry loop makes over its budget was not measured, so the right count is not known. Replacing the window would edit a test file, add a red-first plant and move the expected-counts file, so it needs a builder and an independent review and is not done here. Not measured: per-cell and per-storm run times on a hosted runner, and any stall that has ever ended the injected window.

